      "message": "fix(machine): built-in lathe and mill-turn Z stroke in program coordinates\n\nThe limit check reads travel bands in program coordinates through the\nwork offset (#457). lathe.mch (Z -615..0) and millturn.mch (Z -620..0)\nstated machine-frame bands, so every move in front of the face\n(program Z > 0) - clearance, approach, facing allowance - was out of\nstroke and no turning program posted on either built-in. Restate Z as\nthe full stroke each way (-615..615, -620..620), the convention PR #477\napplies to the mills. X stays 0..R: a lathe X is measured from the\nspindle centreline, which is the program's own X0.\n\nPinned by crates/app/tests/lathe_stroke.rs: a face-and-turn job with\nclearance in front of the face passes and posts on both built-ins; a\nclearance past the stroke still refuses by name and blocks the post.\n\nFixes #493\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
